# The first run of ./runBoxA.sh writes harness.env (gitignored) beside this file
# from its five questions, so copying this one is optional; it documents every
# setting. harness-env.sh sources harness.env BEFORE computing its own defaults,
# so anything set there wins. Every value below is the one the scripts would
# otherwise fall back to; set only what differs.
#
# The original harness's own variables keep their meaning; the kit adds the
# SIZING_* / GUEST_* / DRIVER_* / SERVER_* ones below.

# ============================================================ Box A: the server
# Your skeleton-starter-vaadin-swing-bridge clone. Required.
#SIZING_CLONE_DIR=$HOME/dev/skeleton-starter-vaadin-swing-bridge

# The skeleton-starter revision this kit was exercised against. runBoxA.sh warns when
# the clone differs -- fine, but say so in the run's notes.
#SKELETON_PINNED_REV=53d7028

# The packaged jar (mvn clean package). Default: target/<finalName>.jar, with
# finalName resolved from the clone's pom. Set only if you package elsewhere.
#SIZING_JAR=

# Where your Swing application's jar(s) live. Default: <clone>/applibs
#SIZING_APPLIBS=

# What the kit's view starts. The first run of runBoxA.sh asks for both and installs
# the view (/sizing, view/SizingView.java) in the clone; they reach the server as
# -Dsizing.mainClass / -Dsizing.args, the arguments split on whitespace. A view of
# your own (another VIEW) needs neither.
#SIZING_MAIN_CLASS=com.acme.inventory.Main
#SIZING_ARGS=""

# What runCeiling.sh waits on. Leave at 8088 unless you also change the harness.
#SIZING_PORT=8088

# Your guest jar's manifest Add-Exports / Add-Opens, as flags. DERIVED by every run of
# runBoxA.sh from the jars in applibs (manifestFlags.py) and written into its block,
# because the JVM honours them for `java -jar` only and the bridge launches the guest
# by main class. Set this yourself only to REPLACE the derived list. Space-separated.
#GUEST_MANIFEST_FLAGS=""

# Anything else for the server JVM, space-separated: -Dmyapp.config=/path, or module
# flags your application needs beyond its manifest (JOSM checks for three literal
# --add-exports strings itself). Never -Xmx: the sweep sets it.
#SIZING_EXTRA_JVM=

# Normally resolved from the clone's pom via `mvn help:evaluate`. Set to skip Maven.
#SB_VERSION=1.3.0
#M2_REPO=$HOME/.m2/repository

# How runCeiling.sh finds the server JVM with `jps -l`. For a `java -jar` launch
# jps prints the jar path, so this is the jar's file name (finalName).
# runBoxA.sh writes it; the default matches the unrenamed skeleton.
#SERVER_JPS_MATCH=skeleton-starter-vaadin-swing-bridge

# The server's working directory. Default: the clone.
#SERVER_CWD=$SIZING_CLONE_DIR

# Set (even empty) so runCeiling.sh injects nothing itself: the whole command
# line comes from captureServerArgv.sh. Unset only to run the round-2 JOSM path.
GUEST_JVM_EXTRA=

# The budget, and the heaps runSizing.sh tries: a range of -Xmx values as percentages
# of the budget or as heaps (2g, 2560m), one unit for all three; one cell each by
# default. Or SB_CAPS for an explicit list, which overrides the range.
#BUDGET=4
#SIZING_HEAP_START=60%
#SIZING_HEAP_STOP=80%
#SIZING_HEAP_STEP=10%
#SB_CAPS="2456m 2560m"
# Runs per heap (round-robin), and the cell-count guard: more than this refuses.
#SIZING_REPEATS=1
#SIZING_MAX_CELLS=12

# The @Route of the view the browsers drive: the kit's own is @Route("sizing").
# The skeleton's default @Route("") cannot be addressed. Passed to Box B by
# runBoxA.sh; nothing has to be set on Box B by hand.
#VIEW=sizing

# ============================================================ the scenario
# Your scenario file -- what one user does and what must change on screen (SCENARIO.md).
# Required, no default; the first run of runBoxA.sh writes this line. Copied to Box B
# before each cell, so an edit here needs no further runBoxA.sh run.
#SCENARIO=$HARNESS_HOME/scenario/app-cycle.json
# A data file the scenario needs, if any; the preflight checks it is readable
# (the JOSM example: SCENARIO_DATA=$REPO_ROOT/examples/josm/grid-helsinki.osm).
#SCENARIO_DATA=

# ============================================================ Box B: the load box
# ssh alias for the load box. Keep the address in ~/.ssh/config, not here.
#BOXB=boxb
# The only directory the kit may use on Box B; defaults to its $HOME/dev_load_v2.
#BOXB_ROOT=
# Where runBoxA.sh ships the kit on Box B. Default: this directory's name under
# BOXB_ROOT. Box B needs no git and no credentials; Box A puts the kit there over
# ssh and runs its setup, so the two boxes cannot hold different revisions.
#BOXB_CHECKOUT=$BOXB_ROOT/swingbridge-sizing-kit-dev
BOXB_HARNESS_SUBDIR=harness

# Box B's own harness.env is written by runBoxB.sh when runBoxA.sh runs it there:
# VIEW (from here), and how to launch the driver it built. Nothing to set by hand.

# Only if detection picks the wrong interface on a multi-homed box.
#A_IP=
